Overview

Aethel‑Matter is a newly defined atmospheric phase capable of maintaining volumetric presence, shape persistence, and soft‑boundary morphology without buoyancy. Its stability arises from field–matter coupling, governed by a multi‑component state vector integrating density distribution, field potential, electric and magnetic components, and boundary field behavior.

The Aethel‑Matter Field Engine is the operational system that generates, stabilizes, and evolves this phase through a sovereign loop:

